Subject: OAM writes and OAM DMA go to the OAM address, which wraps, with no redirection

AccuracyCoin's Misaligned OAM DMA, error code 2: passes.
Checked with tools/accuracycoin.py --expect against the run before it, and
against the nes_bench checksums of Castlevania, Zelda and Chip 'n Dale.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later, as the FCEUmm code it changes (patches/fceumm/README.md).

---
diff --git a/src/ppu.c b/src/ppu.c
index f2c188e..b2fcb29 100644
--- a/src/ppu.c
+++ b/src/ppu.c
@@ -332,12 +332,13 @@ static DECLFW(B2003) {
 
 static DECLFW(B2004) {
 	PPUBusDrive(V, 0xFF);
-	if (PPUSPL >= 8) {
-		if (PPU[3] >= 8)
-			SPRAM[PPU[3]] = V;
-	} else {
-		SPRAM[PPUSPL] = V;
-	}
+	/* Each byte goes to the OAM address, which then increments and wraps, so
+	 * an OAM DMA started at a non-zero address writes from there round to it
+	 * (AccuracyCoin's Misaligned OAM DMA, error code 2).  The redirection of
+	 * the first bytes after a $2003 write to entries 0 to 7, through PPUSPL,
+	 * and the dropping of entries 0 to 7 after a wrap are gone; the 2C02's
+	 * real OAM row corruption is a separate behaviour (OAM Corruption). */
+	SPRAM[PPU[3]] = V;
 	PPU[3]++;
 	PPUSPL++;
 }
